#: ../../source/references_composition.md:1
msgid "Composition & Brightness Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:3
msgid ""
"The composable system is the core of visual complexity. It operates at "
"three levels: pixel-level blend modes, multi-grid composition, and "
"adaptive brightness management. This document covers all three, plus the "
"masking/stencil system for spatial control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:5
msgid ""
"**See also:** architecture.md · effects.md · scenes.md · shaders.md · "
"troubleshooting.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:7
msgid "Pixel-Level Blend Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:9
msgid "The `blend_canvas()` Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:11
msgid ""
"All blending operates on full pixel canvases (`uint8 H,W,3`). Internally "
"converts to float32 [0,1] for precision, blends, lerps by opacity, "
"converts back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:24
msgid "20 Blend Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:67
msgid "Blend Mode Selection Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:69
msgid "**Modes that brighten** (safe for dark inputs):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:70
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`screen` — always brightens. Two 50% gray layers screen to 75%. The go-to"
" safe blend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:71
msgid ""
"`add` — simple addition, clips at white. Good for sparkles, glows, "
"particle overlays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:72
msgid ""
"`colordodge` — extreme brightening at overlap zones. Can blow out. Use "
"low opacity (0.3-0.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:73
msgid "`linearlight` — aggressive brightening. Similar to add but with offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:75
msgid "**Modes that darken** (avoid with dark inputs):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:76
msgid ""
"`multiply` — darkens everything. Only use when both layers are already "
"bright."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:77
msgid ""
"`overlay` — darkens when base < 0.5, brightens when base > 0.5. Crushes "
"dark inputs: `2 * 0.12 * 0.12 = 0.03`. Use `screen` instead for dark "
"material."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:78
msgid "`colorburn` — extreme darkening at overlap zones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:80
msgid "**Modes that create contrast**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:81
msgid "`softlight` — gentle contrast. Good for subtle texture overlay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:82
msgid "`hardlight` — strong contrast. Like overlay but keyed on the top layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:83
msgid "`vividlight` — very aggressive contrast. Use sparingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:85
msgid "**Modes that create color effects**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:86
msgid ""
"`difference` — XOR-like patterns. Two identical layers difference to "
"black; offset layers create wild colors. Great for psychedelic looks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:87
msgid ""
"`exclusion` — softer version of difference. Creates complementary color "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:88
msgid ""
"`hard_mix` — posterizes to pure black/white/saturated color at "
"intersections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:90
msgid "**Modes for texture blending**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:91
msgid ""
"`grain_extract` / `grain_merge` — extract a texture from one layer, apply"
" it to another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:93
msgid "Multi-Layer Chaining"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:105
msgid ""
"Order matters: `screen(A, B)` is commutative, but "
"`difference(screen(A,B), C)` differs from `difference(A, screen(B,C))`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:107
msgid "Linear-Light Blend Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:109
msgid ""
"Standard `blend_canvas()` operates in sRGB space — the raw byte values. "
"This is fine for most uses, but sRGB is perceptually non-linear: blending"
" in sRGB darkens midtones and shifts hues slightly. For physically "
"accurate blending (matching how light actually combines), convert to "
"linear light first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:111
msgid ""
"Uses `srgb_to_linear()` / `linear_to_srgb()` from `architecture.md` § "
"OKLAB Color System."
msgstr ""

