#: ../../source/references_composition.md:172
msgid "Multi-Grid Composition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:174
msgid ""
"This is the core visual technique. Rendering the same conceptual scene at"
" different grid densities (character sizes) creates natural texture "
"interference, because characters at different scales overlap at different"
" spatial frequencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:176
msgid "Why It Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:178
msgid "`sm` grid (10pt font): 320x83 characters. Fine detail, dense texture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:179
msgid "`md` grid (16pt): 192x56 characters. Medium density."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:180
msgid "`lg` grid (20pt): 160x45 characters. Coarse, chunky characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_composition.md:182
msgid ""
"When you render a plasma field on `sm` and a vortex on `lg`, then screen-"
"blend them, the fine plasma texture shows through the gaps in the coarse "
"vortex characters. The result has more visual complexity than either "
"layer alone."
msgstr ""

